    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_1X34YGdTiaOe2G2",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID73",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "Q9b6b93ee697a7f59-chunk_dc019f75e9f69c3343645199",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>EDOS Label</strong></p><p><strong>3.4 condescending explanations or unwelcome advice</strong> – Offering unsolicited or patronising advice to women on topics and issues they know more about (known as ‘mansplaining’).</p><br><p><strong>Paragraph</strong></p>Services provided by women’s centres<br><br><table>\n<thead>\n<tr><th>Service</th><th>Yes (countries)</th><th>No (countries)</th><th>Do not know</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Counselling/ psychological support</td><td>39</td><td>1</td><td>6</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Legal advice</td><td>38</td><td>2</td><td>6</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Financial and social welfare support/ advocacy</td><td>29</td><td>6</td><td>11</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Housing advice</td><td>31</td><td>4</td><td>11</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Employment</td><td>22</td><td>10</td><td>14</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Referrals/collaboration with other services</td><td>38</td><td>1</td><td>7</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Representation at court/ police/social services/ etc.</td><td>30</td><td>7</td><td>9</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Residential support services (e.g., emergency accommodation)</td><td>25</td><td>9</td><td>12</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">\n\nTable 10: Services provided by women’s centres\n\nAccording to the 2024 data, counselling and psychological support are available in 39 countries (85%), making this the most widespread service provided by women’s centres. Both individual and group counselling are provided, often grounded in trauma-informed and empowerment-based approaches.</div><br>",
        "DataExportTag": "Q9b6b93ee697a7f59-chunk_dc019f75e9f69c3343645199",
